{
  "requirement": "The SDK interns the node data returned by `Domain::source_node` for the `OutlineData`. `Domain::node_content` returns that node’s contents. Mapping and read failures return errors. Agents use the node reference from discovery with `read_node`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests cover every obligation in `read_source.behavior`.\n\n**Obligations**\n1. The SDK interns the node data that `Domain::source_node` returns for the `OutlineData`.\n2. `Domain::node_content` returns that node's contents.\n3. Mapping failures return errors.\n4. Read failures return errors.\n5. Agents use the node reference from discovery with `read_node`.\n\n**Coverage**\n- **Mapping errors:** `agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[direct_source_reads_preserve_mapping_errors_and_record_only_successful_returns]` uses two addresses that the test `Domain::source_node` rejects: an unknown path and an unknown selector. It asserts the error text \"unsupported source item\". It also asserts that no dependency was recorded and that `node_content` was never called (`reads == 0`, `read_nodes` empty).\n- **Read errors:** the same test sets `fail_read` and asserts the \"prepared source read failed\" error and that no dependency was recorded.\n- **Interning and contents:** after the failure flag is cleared, a read of the supported address returns \"prepared contents\". The dependency node equals `intern_node(\"source-node\")`, which is the string `source_node` returned. The test domain's `node_content` records the node data it receives, and the test asserts `read_nodes == [\"source-node\",\"source-node\"]`. That shows `node_content` was called with the interned node that `source_node` mapped. The helper `fn[node_content]` and `fn[source_node]` in the test domain confirm this.\n- **Agents use the discovery node reference with `read_node`:** `agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions]` runs an agent through `list_sources`. It calls `read_node` with an unknown node and asserts \"invalid node ID\". It then calls `read_node` with the node entry taken from the discovery listing and asserts the text is \"a source snapshot\". It also asserts that the on-disk contents are not returned, and it runs this twice as independent executions.\n- **Other tests:** the `read_source` tests in `agent/tests.rs` and `fn[search_excerpts_redact_credentials_before_serialization_and_paging]` give further coverage of reads, dependency recording, and discovery staying separate from reads. They support the main tests above but are not needed for adequacy.\n\nNo gap is found, and there are no acknowledgments to assess.",
  "references": "8dd8de79d0a6e3d8d5666c2c2e12294450569d5291c27a71be57931f922895b0",
